# Local work archive — September 24, 2026

This tag replaces 20 temporary backup branches. It preserves unfinished local work as it existed when backed up; it is not a release or an integration into main.

The snapshots.json file maps each original branch or worktree to its saved commit. All listed commits are parents of this archive commit, so Git retains their files and history when this tag is fetched.

To recover work in a separate checkout:

```sh
git fetch origin tag archive/local-work-2026-09-24
git show archive/local-work-2026-09-24:snapshots.json
git worktree add -b codex/recover-local-work ../Pundits-recovered <commit-from-snapshots.json>
```

The `worktrees/workspace` entry contains the main local working-directory snapshot. Some historical worktrees contain unresolved conflicts or missing files; these were saved verbatim. Ignored credentials, dependencies, and build caches were excluded.
